# Exemplos de chamadas para o perfil local (REST Client do VS Code ou HTTP Client do IntelliJ).
# Tokens sintéticos em src/main/resources/application-local.yml.
# Preço sintético do SKU-n: 10,00 + (n mod 50) x 2,50. SKU-0001 = 12,50; SKU-0042 = 115,00.

@base = http://localhost:8080
@chave = 0b9f4c7e-6a2d-4f5b-9a51-3c1e7d2f8a10

### v2: criação (201)
# @name criacao
POST {{base}}/v2/orders
Authorization: Bearer token-cliente-ana
Idempotency-Key: {{chave}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer": { "customerId": "c-10293", "name": "Cliente Sintético", "email": "cliente@exemplo.com" },
  "items": [ { "sku": "SKU-0001", "quantity": 2 }, { "sku": "SKU-0042", "quantity": 1 } ],
  "expectedTotal": { "amount": "140.00", "currency": "BRL" }
}

### v2: repetição com a mesma chave e o mesmo corpo (201 com Idempotent-Replayed: true, mesmo pedido)
POST {{base}}/v2/orders
Authorization: Bearer token-cliente-ana
Idempotency-Key: {{chave}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer": { "customerId": "c-10293", "name": "Cliente Sintético", "email": "cliente@exemplo.com" },
  "items": [ { "sku": "SKU-0001", "quantity": 2 }, { "sku": "SKU-0042", "quantity": 1 } ],
  "expectedTotal": { "amount": "140.00", "currency": "BRL" }
}

### v2: mesma chave com corpo diferente (422 idempotency-key-reuse)
POST {{base}}/v2/orders
Authorization: Bearer token-cliente-ana
Idempotency-Key: {{chave}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer": { "customerId": "c-10293", "name": "Cliente Sintético", "email": "cliente@exemplo.com" },
  "items": [ { "sku": "SKU-0001", "quantity": 3 } ]
}

### v2: sem Idempotency-Key (400)
POST {{base}}/v2/orders
Authorization: Bearer token-cliente-ana
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer": { "customerId": "c-10293", "name": "Cliente Sintético", "email": "cliente@exemplo.com" },
  "items": [ { "sku": "SKU-0001", "quantity": 1 } ]
}

### v2: total esperado divergente (409 price-changed)
POST {{base}}/v2/orders
Authorization: Bearer token-cliente-ana
Idempotency-Key: 6a1f0c3e-2b4d-4e8f-9a7b-1c2d3e4f5a6b
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer": { "customerId": "c-10293", "name": "Cliente Sintético", "email": "cliente@exemplo.com" },
  "items": [ { "sku": "SKU-0001", "quantity": 1 } ],
  "expectedTotal": { "amount": "10.00", "currency": "BRL" }
}

### v2: consulta do pedido criado
GET {{base}}/v2/orders/{{criacao.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer token-cliente-ana

### v2: pedido de outro chamador (404)
GET {{base}}/v2/orders/{{criacao.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer token-cliente-bruno

### v1: consumidor atual, sem header (201; comportamento da 1.0.0)
POST {{base}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer token-erp
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerId": "c-555", "items": [ { "sku": "SKU-0001", "quantity": 1 } ] }

### v1: com Idempotency-Key opcional, pelo alias /v1/orders
POST {{base}}/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer token-erp
Idempotency-Key: 3c9e2a10-7d4b-4f61-8e2a-5b6c7d8e9f01
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerId": "c-555", "items": [ { "sku": "SKU-0001", "quantity": 1 } ] }

### v1: repetição pela rota /orders (mesma operação: 201 com Idempotent-Replayed: true)
POST {{base}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer token-erp
Idempotency-Key: 3c9e2a10-7d4b-4f61-8e2a-5b6c7d8e9f01
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerId": "c-555", "items": [ { "sku": "SKU-0001", "quantity": 1 } ] }

### Consulta cruzada: pedido criado pela v2, lido pela v1 pelo legacyId
GET {{base}}/orders/{{criacao.response.body.legacyId}}
Authorization: Bearer token-cliente-ana
